      "The Data Governance Act (applying since September 2023) created a regime for trusted data intermediaries and data altruism. The Commission forecast EUR 7-11 billion for the data economy by 2028, but uptake has been modest - 38 registered intermediaries and 7 altruism organisations by mid-2026 - and many countries were late in setting up authorities. Legal scholars argued the rules could make intermediaries unviable, and in November 2025 the Commission proposed folding the DGA into the Data Act and making the intermediary regime voluntary.",
